2186045417] [17592186167338 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\n$\\int \\frac{9}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167338 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5b4813f8-fe53-5ee3-84e5-ae77d604d4d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167338 #edb/ref 1074 "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{9}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=9\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=9\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167395 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360405 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167395 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95645" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167395 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167395 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\n$\\int (\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167395 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f2fa6c48-e221-5b5f-83d3-bc5955c5483f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167395 #edb/ref 1074 "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =4\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167396 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186165584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167396 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95655" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167396 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167396 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nCalculate $\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{5(1-{x}^{2})}+3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x$ for $|x|<1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167396 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8a56431e-73ba-50fb-96c9-b7316cca361e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167396 #edb/ref 1074 "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{5(1-{x}^{2})}+3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{5}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+{x}^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167590 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167590 #edb/ref 1061 31170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167590 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "347cc1c3-4cbd-529a-b4ed-0b7d416fe5dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167590 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167591 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167591 #edb/ref 1061 31171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167591 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "92682fd2-413d-5454-86c3-241d087214d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167591 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166759 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167592 #edb/ref 1061 31172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167592 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a07e3608-4411-5b20-a3f8-e14096686e80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167592 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167703 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167590 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167703 #edb/ref 1061 32697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167703 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e1dbdeed-56c4-580b-a139-6581eed4ac8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167703 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186168093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168093 #edb/ref 1064 "Recall the following derivatives of the inverse hyperbolic functions:\n$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}, &  & \\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}, &  & \\,x\\in (1,\\infty ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x) & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}, &  & \\,x\\in (-1,1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince integration is the reverse of differentiation, we arrive at the following basic integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x+C, &  & \\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ) \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x+C, &  & \\,x\\in (1,\\infty ) \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+C, &  & \\,x\\in (-1,1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now use these formulas for finding integrals. For example, let's find the integral\n\n$$\n\\int \\left(\\dfrac{5}{2\\sqrt{x^2-1}} + 2x \\right) \\textrm d x\n$$\n\nUsing the properties of integration and the formulas above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}+2x)\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x+{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168093 #edb/ref 1065 5212 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168093 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "35388b84-1b96-58fb-b1e8-46477370aa96" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168093 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045