erbolic sine function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360610 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360610 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95639" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360610 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360610 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\n$\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}+1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360610 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "57a86446-8a8a-579c-ab6b-0108201455ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360610 #edb/ref 1074 "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}+1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=(\\sqrt{2}+1)\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=(\\sqrt{2}+1)\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360611 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360611 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95642" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360611 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360611 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\n$\\int (\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}})\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360611 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2ed2766f-124b-5427-8fb1-ae118be1949d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360611 #edb/ref 1074 "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}})\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-5\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
